&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Program Manager (m/f/d) to drive planning, delivery, and operational excellence across our engineering department. You will work with cross-functional programs, coordinating and building the operating rhythms that keep teams aligned, and turning technical progress into clear, decision-ready insights for leadership.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own end-to-end program planning and delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;for the department, coordinating cross-functional initiatives spanning multiple engineering disciplines (e.g., hardware, electronics, software, controls, and test &amp;amp; validation).&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coordinate delivery milestones across teams&lt;/strong&gt;, tracking cross-functional dependencies, surfacing and resolving blockers, and ensuring alignment at every program milestone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run the department&#39;s business review cadence&lt;/strong&gt;, preparing and driving monthly reviews covering organizational goals — synthesizing technical progress, risks, and dependencies into executive-ready insights for senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and maintain a single source of truth&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;for all programs in Jira, establishing program frameworks, operating cadences, and visibility tools for cross-functional partners on bi-weekly and monthly cycles.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and run a resource planning framework&lt;/strong&gt;, leading regular reviews to align team capacity with evolving program requirements and technical workload.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage budget and OPEX tracking&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;for the department, enabling data-driven monthly trade-off decisions in response to shifting priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in technical program management, engineering operations, or a similar role within an engineering organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Proven track record coordinating cross-functional programs across multiple engineering disciplines and bringing rigor and structure to them.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Strong command of program management tools (Jira, Confluence, Sharepoint) and data/reporting tools.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience establishing operating cadences, business reviews (MBR/QBR), and single-source-of-truth systems from the ground up and roadmap.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with resource/capacity planning and budget or OPEX tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, with the ability to distill complex technical topics into clear narratives for senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering background or degree strongly preferred; comfort navigating deeply technical discussions is essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Experience in robotics, mechatronics, or other multi-disciplinary engineering environments.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting or reporting directly to department or executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Familiarity with both agile (software) and waterfall (hardware) delivery methodologies.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
